<title>SWEDEN: Riksbank interevenes to support crown - dealers.</title>
<headline>Riksbank interevenes to support crown - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, intervened on the currency market in support of the crown during the morning trading session, dealers said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The Riksbank declined to comment.</p>
<p>Dealers said the bank had intervened at 4.35 versus the mark. The crown slipped steadily throughout the morning from its late Monday fix of 4.3260.</p>
<p>At 1220 GTM, the crown was trading at 4.3470.</p>
<p>The Riksbank has said it would intervene on the currency markets to stabilise the crown, although it declined to specify whether or not it had a pre-determined target level.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
